This applies the secant iteration until consecutive iterates differ by at most the tolerance $e$.

Since the population is measured in millions, an accuracy of a thousand individuals is a tolerance of $0.001$ million. We solve

$$
f(x_4)-2=0.
$$

```matlab
f = @(x) 7*x.*exp(-x);
g = @(x) f(x) - 2;

p = 0.1;
q = 1.0;
e = 0.001;

while abs(q-p) > e
    r = q - g(q)*(q-p)/(g(q)-g(p));
    p = q;
    q = r;
end

x4 = q;
```

This gives the smaller positive solution $x_4 \approx 0.407$ million. Depending on the starting values, the larger positive solution $x_4 \approx 2.492$ million may also be found.
